the clark county division of family  services the sponsors of this next  segment is doing what they can to help  the foster youth in our area here's how  you can support during national foster  care month and beyond  foster care is a cause that the clark  county division of family services tends  to year round but especially in may may  is national foster care month and this  is a time that we are able to bring  attention to the need for foster  families for our foster youth and care  we currently have in clark county 3 000  children in foster care and less than  500 foster families available for them  and for potential foster families  jennifer erbs and her team are here for  you so we are currently here at our  resource center  this is where we provide foster parents  with their initial training  our foster parent champions are here at  this facility as well and in the same  location is peggy's attic which is our  donation center which allows us to  provide  initial clothing for foster parents who  first get a placement  we  have opportunities to sign up for an  information session at  clarkcountyfostercare.com  if you're interested just to hear the  information about what you need to  become a foster parent and who is  qualified to become a foster parent so  to become a foster parent you really  just need to have some patience and  understanding of some trauma that some  of our kids are going to go through  you have to be at least 21 years old to  be a foster parent  you can be single or married you can be  in an lgbtq relationship  you can live in a condo  rental or own your own home  you're able to  have transportation to be able to get  our kids to and from the needed  appointments for them  you have to take nine weeks of training  pass some background clearances  and have our workers come out to your  home to do a home study  to make sure that we're getting quality  families for our kids once you pass your  training the help from the division of  family services does not stop there we  have foster parent champions who are  foster parents  currently or have been foster parents  that you can call and they can help walk  you through a crisis or refer you to  services in the community  peggy's attic again is a great resource  for  clothing we also have hannah's closet  which is a partner in the community  also  to help with  clothing or additional resources our  licensing workers are available to call  if you have questions if there's  concerns about what's going on in a case  we're available to  meet with our families quarterly were  available for them  any other time that they need questions  answered regarding their kids and of  course fostering is a huge commitment so  if you're not ready or able but still  want to give back to foster youth you  can donating to peggy's addict being a  mentor for kids you can be a casa worker  where you can volunteer  and help kids through their foster care  journey you can also support the  division of family services special art  project by local artist darian deenan  the project is traveling throughout  clark county spreading awareness about  our traveling foster youth starting in  may and going all the way through the  summer so the exhibit visualizes the  wishes of children currently in foster  care and those in need of a foster home  so at the end of the day the number one  qualification for a foster parent is  love our our children are traumatized  they have to be ripped out of a home  that they  thought was their own  and they have to be placed into a  stranger's home and so understanding  what that must feel like for a child is  really important  thank you to the clark county division  of family services for sponsoring this  segment for more information call 702  702-455-0181  or visit clarkcountyfostercare.com
 

